The question in your screenshot is about TCP RST (Reset). To understand it properly, you need to know the different TCP flags (control commands), their functions, and how they are used in network communication.

### 1\. TCP commands (TCP flags) and their functions

TCP flags control how a TCP connection is established, maintained and terminated.

![An Introduction to Port Scanning for Beginners Using Nmap | by Angelina Salim | Medium](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/NkxfHJ4Wc6oiTmeQz6wErT4rgTIDOwY4jUXCYxUWgkm8pwnqfTrlotWF-ql3eu53pfS1K9OJnLfqGTX3x6LUnXSgE2P5u2ynkbHwI_CEH8RvJSm5CdaQK1s0A-5a4DVGmfgYH1GMcRxqiLHhLtGhbUm8Xv1nR-lw9nAhSfqKpnhxzH1wBXTFNshvEgepkJ-_?purpose=fullsize)

1\. SYN – Synchronize

* Function: Starts a TCP connection.

* How it is used: A client sends SYN to request a connection with a server.

* Example: Your browser requests a connection to a website.

![PPT - PART 5 Transport Layer PowerPoint Presentation, free download - ID:5403249](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/EzFBdA39QyrkpZe3Xl__ioDkmgR3rSJYCIDyzbsHLkQbiMTBKaAFlyF_CWiVLsKveLLZMXyqjbITlCsma7LRnbdZlKgS8q8l1CaHrqkJ_JNZo6sAYwce2oBg44vIlkfYLNgGiYdmz0yZ396dwL_osDW6sHdG2lgqCXR-qtgZaDGvmpyqqKa3v-S7MBjaUHmV?purpose=fullsize)

2\. ACK – Acknowledgment

* Function: Confirms that data has been received.

* How it is used: The receiving device sends ACK to acknowledge received TCP data.

* Example: A server acknowledges data sent by your computer.

![Everything You Always Wanted to Know About TCP But Too Afraid to Ask](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/sNXXnfanLXdAHNLPSdSl8up51kfq5GEPJZ_ahBe20Ix4uLRObTxBd6VishmyE2g-BdGPU-lUcq4e0N3_JX8qjdJg9H9rYUQ5gziOHYJ9Sfp-XgJRPyK_ZjtXOIYZghgHeUqKoeFyWqNWMoRSbhvgxvS6AEmj1oTdDd38WINvVeyQsTaO2_TbaJqzJSC_P-M8?purpose=fullsize)

3\. FIN – Finish

* Function: Closes a TCP connection gracefully.

* How it is used: One device sends FIN when it has finished sending data.

* Example: Closing a completed web connection.

![TCP RESET Flag | CYBRESCUE](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/QFL6UHxFzzBVXUfrJ0RjsjN0uq802CbEEaywOtVk076Ot31nIJ37HmUmzrhjZKL1rcc70BnWNBtiIuvq-SUWJpw2VUZEqfuxuFHTkHdOidlG01yld53zo5GWv9H3ttYzx8TjG5sxW2bojjYfdKuDAWHdbuD6Rz7l6OtxG3GCNzFeJOvHRie1d0_M--YgdrTQ?purpose=fullsize)

4\. RST – Reset

* Function: Immediately resets or aborts a TCP connection.

* How it is used: A device sends RST when a connection is invalid or cannot continue.

* Example: A server rejects a connection request.

