5\. PSH – Push

* Function: Requests that received data be delivered promptly to the application.

* How it is used: Sent with data when prompt delivery is desired.

* Example: Interactive communication.

![Cisco Learning Network](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/TCSi88HV8DhBTCdYpTYQ6UddH12rLwvTTJ7Do7y4RQhl3sQohn7QwDbU3dI6GeL5dKAT9OthoMqntwbHmpRuzV7GSEi4DWNuXJxMGEiaqXTYX7awKSpg5-FDJFei-XZmJdJhrRaCbeQU0ZieFd8sP0ofHwi7KDLMD7FAwvR699R41P5bcmkhyGvOQmCHzhhS?purpose=fullsize)

6\. URG – Urgent

* Function: Indicates that the urgent pointer field is significant.

* How it is used: Marks urgent data in a TCP segment.

* Example: Special urgent-data handling by an application.

![PPT - Explicit Congestion Notification (ECN) PowerPoint Presentation, free download - ID:2327271](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/BltJtGEM0tH63CnOfdvnq6uWMfCsCK39zViuRTM4fOhqzsCTaSrTR7zcKmlYiJtChgPajyBXmslK8FGVQixmFcXfDikLfkWwvBEznu5hOOl5VlEeXFHJZyFbjmk3BiYaqNsr5Kjj29eQ21hJd6b9VD4T7Et3WlsnNPpaGI2iqgdgXdf-zYsQTIkafRwH3eCC?purpose=fullsize)

7\. ECE – ECN Echo

* Function: Indicates congestion notification information.

* How it is used: Helps communicate network congestion without necessarily dropping packets.

![PPT - 15-744: Computer Networking PowerPoint Presentation, free download - ID:9205612](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/G9SgjE5iyW10U6Ey9eCFedT8Wzt1-zCWWv7LGaBjgMNxVOx4jxRQfM0zNaNY7Otd4Ew3EXhR4KA9CBx2Qd5hJqwF2QNJ0HdsUaUvCt7hSHUetNCApMOUmlweMZ3Zq6gXuvcpHSZ-tj1ujWX6wVvgtqFLjUSVRShWzZnuiq6KpkBxa5Y4NqLVlXMbN_VglSJP?purpose=fullsize)

8\. CWR – Congestion Window Reduced

* Function: Indicates that the sender has reduced its congestion window.

* How it is used: Helps TCP respond to network congestion.

9\. NS – Nonce Sum

* Function: An older ECN-related flag.

* How it is used: Originally designed to support protection of ECN feedback information.

### 2\. How TCP flags work together

The most important process is the TCP three-way handshake.

![he Complete Journey of a Web Request: DNS, TCP, HTTPS | Medium](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/cdIDkjUOf8LPxy2u7HuX0ymX_stEOGZEYzlY-OnhCChy2xljzHtJDSRWm9BUEa7eSAczMcjhfrZLZfdRQvY1vRFfDW5ZtHZ6ZCQZ6FsJHVx8cb7rjl0aY3qzN470gSToGnQUc8CwKm1M-AZ8zD_zw1XkzI59zR74yU5m-C1qCl041a6WPatxCIr-7MDDO67C?purpose=fullsize)

| Step | Command   | Function                        |
| ---- | --------- | ------------------------------- |
| 1    | SYN       | Client requests connection      |
| 2    | SYN + ACK | Server accepts and acknowledges |
| 3    | ACK       | Client confirms connection      |

After this process, communication can begin.

To close a connection:

